    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30899" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶἑν</span></b>  (for the aspiration, found in cod. Rav.
		of <i><span class="en">
			Ar.
		</span></i>, etc., cf. <i><span class="en">
			A.D.
			<u>Synt.</u>
			319.26
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>An.Bachm.</u>
			1.208
		</span></i>), Particle used in dialogue and oratory, in passing to the next
		point, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>well, quite so, very
				good</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				1075
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ap.</u>
				19a
			</span></i>, etc.; "
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶἑν" ἐρῶ καὶ κατανεύσομαι καὶ
					ἀνανεύσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>R.</u>
					35o
				</span></i>
			e: folld. by a question, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				176
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶἑν: τί δῆτα</span> .
			. ; <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1308
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶἑν: καὶ δὴ τεθνᾶσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					386
				</span></i>
			: folld. by imper., <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				534
			</span></i>; in argument, <i>so far so good</i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶἑν, ἐρεῖ δέ</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				4.2.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶἑν, τοῦτο μὲν ἡμῖν κείσθω:
				ἔφαμεν δέ</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				350d
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶἑν, ἀλλὰ νὴ Δία</span> .
			. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				20.75
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i> Chr.<i><span class="en">
				17.19
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶἑν δή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					213e
				</span></i>
			. [At the beginning of a trimeter, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶἑν, ἀκούω</span>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				657
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				663
			</span></i>: extra versum in <i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i> l.c.]</div>
